# Critical: data/ must NOT be baked into the image. Docker initializes a
# freshly-created named volume from whatever exists at that path in the
# image at container start -- if data/wb_dashboard.sqlite3 were copied in
# here, every brand-new client would start out with a copy of whoever's
# data happened to be in this build context (e.g. demo/test data from
# development) instead of a genuinely empty database. app.py's own
# init_db() creates a correct empty schema on first boot into the empty
# mounted volume; nothing here should pre-populate it.
data/

tests/
__pycache__/
*.pyc
.venv/
.git/
*.md
